From ad01fd239ed0f14210fe3d8407d218f849698f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:20:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] Economy wallet: confirm smart-account routed payments,
 wait out wallet lag, keep the hash visible

From the owner's first real top-up (order 0x4121e687..., tx 0x9c62...b08f):
- MetaMask routed the pay call through its Delegation Manager (redeemDelegations),
  so the mined tx's to/input differ from the request although the call ran. The
  wallet's own returned hash now counts as done when the receipt carries exactly
  the intended effect (Approval / Paid / Staked / Withdrawn from the intended
  contract, this sender, this call's arguments). Pasted hashes never get this.
  Replaying the real receipt: confirmed at once (was NOT_FINALIZED, then REPLACED).
- MetaMask answers eth_getTransactionByHash from its own copy (no block, no chain
  ID) while it still lists a mined tx as pending; that raced the receipt and showed
  TRANSACTION_MISMATCH. Such a record is now polled again instead of judged.
- send() shows the broadcast hash before the context check, so a session refresh
  during the wallet prompt no longer leaves "wallet response uncertain" with no
  hash and no "check original transaction" button.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
